Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
; VibeForge Systems - Windows Environment Bundle
; explorer.reg - File Explorer baselines (per-user, HKCU)
;
; Developer-friendly Explorer defaults plus the Windows 10 "classic" right-click
; context menu on Windows 11. All values are per-user and reversible.
;
; TO REVERT:
;   - File extension / hidden-file toggles: set the values back to their
;     defaults (HideFileExt=1, Hidden=2) or change them in Folder Options.
;   - Classic context menu: delete the CLSID key below, then restart Explorer.
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\Advanced]
; Show known file extensions (0 = show). Essential for dev work.
"HideFileExt"=dword:00000000
; Show hidden files and folders (1 = show).
"Hidden"=dword:00000001
; Open File Explorer to "This PC" instead of Quick Access (1 = This PC).
"LaunchTo"=dword:00000001
; Show the full path in the title bar / address bar.
"FullPath"=dword:00000001
; Keep protected operating-system files hidden: 0 = hidden (default, safer);
; 1 would reveal them. We deliberately keep the safe default.
"ShowSuperHidden"=dword:00000000

; --- Restore the Windows 10 classic right-click context menu -----------------
; An empty default value under this CLSID's InprocServer32 tells Windows 11 to
; fall back to the full classic context menu (no "Show more options" step).
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\CLSID\{86ca1aa0-34aa-4e8b-a509-50c905bae2a2}\InprocServer32]
@=""
